  "lineage": "TCP congestion-control lineage, the SUCCESSOR: Reno keeps Tahoe's slow start/avoidance and adds fast retransmit on three duplicate ACKs and fast recovery (halve cwnd instead of collapsing to one segment). 'Reno' is the name later analyses (Fall & Floyd 1996) attach to this behaviour; NewReno, SACK, CUBIC descend from it. Preserved from unix-history-repo tag BSD-4_3_Reno.",
